<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xml:id="diaMuertos-ws-rooms">
  <title>Rooms</title>

  <page>
    <exercise xml:id="ex-rooms-gato-floor" workspace="6cm">
      <title>The Gato Floor</title>
      <statement>
        <sidebyside widths="70% 10%" margins="0% 10%">
          <stack>
            <p>The people at the fiesta play a game and only allow certain músicos to enter a given floor of the house.</p>
            <p>For example, <q>Only músicos that are Gatos!</q></p>
          </stack>
          <image source="diaMuertos-Gato.png" decorative="yes"/>
        </sidebyside>
        <p>
          <ol>
            <li><p>Give an example of three different músicos that can enter the Gato floor.</p></li>
            <li><p>How many músicos can enter the Gato floor?</p></li>
            <li><p>What percentage of all músicos are <alert>G</alert>atos? How can you visualize it?</p></li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-rooms-gato-suit-room" workspace="6cm">
      <title>The Gato + Suit Room</title>
      <statement>
        <sidebyside widths="45% 40%" margins="0% 5%">
          <p>Now, inside the Gato floor, there is a room called <q>Only gatos that wear suit (pants).</q></p>
          <image source="diaMuertos-Gato+Suit.png" decorative="yes" width="40%"/>
        </sidebyside>
        <ol>
          <li><p>What is a mathematical question that you could ask about this room? Write at least two questions.</p></li>
          <li><p>How can you visualize this room?</p></li>
          <li><p>Answer your questions!</p></li>
        </ol>
      </statement>
    </exercise>
  </page>

  <page>
    <exercise xml:id="ex-rooms-your-own-room" workspace="6cm">
      <title>Your own room</title>
      <statement>
        <p>Work in pairs. Create your own special room, writing a <alert>precise condition</alert> for accessing that room. Challenge other pairs to represent this room and find the maximum number of músicos inside!</p>
        <p>Bonus: do the different rooms overlap? How?</p>
      </statement>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>
